  note over BOOT
    Nested quoting preserves backslashes and
    apostrophes through each Fish command layer.
    Pure fixtures establish string round trips,
    not shell syntax, so the operator command
    checks Fish syntax before fetching its helper.
  end note

  FISH -> FILES : parent exclusively creates bootstrap evidence\nno mkdir -p/reuse/overwrite/deletion
  FISH -> FISH : GNU timeout TERM 895s + KILL grace 5s\nworker budget <=900s; host fish -n before fetch

  note over FISH
    The outer Fish parent survives worker timeout
    so exit capture retains the actual status.
    Its deadline includes a termination grace,
    not another workload allowance or proof
    of physical host containment.
  end note

  FISH -> FISH : existing Bun 1.4.0, gh, Fish, GNU tar/coreutils\nMise auto-install false; no login/config/install
  FISH -> GH : one plaintext contents GET at actual helper OID\nTERM 55s + KILL grace 5s, hostname github.com
  GH --> FISH : retain source/exit; <=128 KiB post-fetch soft cap\nverify fixed SHA before Bun --no-env-file --no-install
  FISH -> RECEIVE : --approved-host-receive-1 + actual helper OID\nstandalone imports node: only
  RECEIVE -> FILES : pinned Cargo.lock/Bun preflight\nexclusive receive evidence + fresh workspace/context\n>=8 GiB free; workspace <=8 GiB soft usage
  RECEIVE -> RECEIVE : child environment removes TAR_OPTIONS only\nno global environment/configuration mutation

  note over RECEIVE,TAR
    The tar environment can request extra commands
    outside this bounded archive extraction.
    Removing its options only in the child
    preserves the global configuration while
    keeping the existing extractor in use.
  end note

  group Two asset GETs share one shrinking 600s deadline
    RECEIVE -> GH : manifest asset ID 730048215 FIRST\n868,843 bytes + exact fixed SHA-256
    GH --> RECEIVE : retained bytes/digest/exit, then deadline check
    RECEIVE -> RECEIVE : validate assetSourceCommit f3e277d + bundle identity\n3,939 manifest rows/native65/offline limitation
    RECEIVE -> GH : bundle asset ID 730047564 SECOND\n140,694,281 bytes + exact fixed SHA-256
    GH --> RECEIVE : retained bytes/digest/exit, then deadline check\nlast download cannot reset or escape the deadline
  end

  note over RECEIVE
    A failed write can leave only part of a chunk
    in the retained command output.
    Hashing completed write operations preserves
    evidence of the bytes, rather than describing
    data that the filesystem never accepted.
  end note

  group Listing, extraction and verification share 180s within total 900s
    RECEIVE -> TAR : standard GNU tar -t / gzip, bounded listing\nexact unique set = manifest rows UNION five roots
    TAR --> RECEIVE : list <=2 MiB; mismatch stops before extraction
